{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274995-umbral-spirits","id":1274995,"title":"Umbral spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-17T18:53:08-08:00","id":1274995,"title":"Umbral spirits","content":"I am working on NPC vampire and need help with something. Part of the vampire's story is he once had mage friends and they were set to go into the umbra to find a cure for his vampirism. But then the Avatar Storm happened - just before the vampire joined them. The mages all died horribly. The vampire had a sad. In any case, I'm trying to find out what spirits or creatures might have been powerful enough to restore life to the vampire, and negotiable enough to ask.<br /> <br /> Suggestions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T19:06:52-08:00","id":1274998,"title":"","content":"Within canon, magically vampirism is reversed by Maimonides and I think this is the only canon time the curse is reversed outside of Gehenna. Needless to say, it's rare and if it were doable viable the umbra it probably would have happened or been brought up.<br /> <br /> In your chronicle, if the curse of Caine is truly brought by God you'll need some reason it can be reversed. Given that, you're looking at a power level of Incarna (very powerful) or Celestine (obscenely powerful). Celestines are almost never interacted with directly in the same way one doesn't visit the sun. Alternatively, a very potent demon could likely do it but entities powerful enough to do this could only be compelled to act by someone also potent enough to do it.<br /> <br /> Another option: If you're in a game with the avatar storm, the psychopomps have the ability to manipulate avatars so it may be easier to call upon one of these entities to do it. There's no canon proof that they can reverse the curse of Caine but they can at least directly manipulate avatars, so that's a start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T19:12:41-08:00","id":1274999,"title":"","content":"Another option, if you wanted, would be the kith art of Naming. At level 5 you can edit true names which is written as being able to change fundamental aspects of an entity. This Art is almost solely practiced by the Sidhe and a very small number of Eshu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T19:26:52-08:00","id":1275001,"title":"","content":"Most it is supposed to be a bit of tragic backs story. The Vampire In Question once ran with one of those multi-splat groups, and it featured mages and vampires, and possibly others. This group was supposed to go on a Great Quest to see [fill in the blank], a creature that could cure vampirism. And then it went to Hell with the Avatar storm, and the Vampire In Question was the only survivor. That was 20 years ago. I just want to keep the name straight on what this party was seeking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T05:44:54-08:00","id":1275065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274995-umbral-spirits?p=1274998#post1274998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within canon, magically vampirism is reversed by Maimonides and I think this is the only canon time the curse is reversed outside of Gehenna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also by Osiris. He restored the humanity of some of his Children (and killed the rest) as part of Mummy revised plot. <br /> <br /> But, yes, I would say that we're looking at a &quot;power level&quot; Incarna+. I would look at spirits that have a symbolic relationship with vampires.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> * The Sun it's antithetical to vampirism and usually kills them. Perhaps a powerful avatar of Helios could burn the Curse w/o killing the vampire. Perhaps the vampire troupe knew that the Children of Osiris were cured and reasoned that if Osiris can then Ra should be able to do the same.<br /> <br /> * You can find the spirits of the Archangels in the Heavens of the Astral Umbra. Nodism postulates that the Archangels cursed Caine when he refused to repent, perhaps by finding them a vampire could choose the redemption that Caine rejected. <br /> <br /> Both are spirits that would be very hard to aproach as a lone vampire, not just 'cause they're on the Umbra but also because vampire nature impedes to reach them. One it's in the frigging Sun, and Heaven it's a Realm very hard to reach for anyone, the impulses of the Beast probably don't make it any easier. Having a mixed party would help a lot with such a seeking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}